Scope of this license
---------------------
The complete standard MIT notice above is the authoritative licence text (it
is the "MIT notice body" reproduced once in the manuscript's S1 code-licence
box, per the Phase E manuscript-drafting plan). This section only records
which files it covers; it is not part of the notice.

This MIT license covers the teaching *code* of the Track 1 chapter, namely:

  * every `*.py` file under `examples/chapter/`;
  * `examples/__init__.py` and `examples/legacy/__init__.py`;
  * `scripts/extract_listings.py`, `scripts/gen_topic_embeddings.py`,
    `scripts/lint_manuscript.py`, and `scripts/build_manuscript.py`;
  * `tests/chapter_examples/test_extract_listings.py` and
    `tests/chapter_examples/test_manuscript_lint.py`; and
  * the eight golden-fixture files under
    `tests/chapter_examples/fixtures/manuscript_expand/`
    (`listing_in.md`, `listing.expected.md`, `assignment_in.md`,
    `assignment.expected.md`, `figure_in.md`, `figure.expected.md`,
    `refs_in.md`, `refs.expected.md`).

It does NOT cover:
  * `examples/legacy/*.py` (pre-existing charting/chunking code, out of the
    scope of Phase E.2b and licensed separately by the wider project);
  * `*.md` files **under `examples/chapter/`** and everything under
    `examples/chapter/data/` -- those are covered by
    `examples/chapter/LICENSE-CONTENT` (CC BY 4.0). (This exclusion is scoped
    to `examples/chapter/`; the eight `*.md` golden-fixture files listed above,
    which live under `tests/`, ARE covered by this MIT licence.)
  * everything under `manuscript/` -- see `manuscript/LICENSE-NOTES.md`.
  * `.gitattributes` (repo root) -- repo configuration that enforces this
    material's LF line-ending requirement; it is recorded in
    `manuscript/LICENSE-NOTES.md` and is not itself licensed as code.
